-- Old Age Security Act, PART III, sections 22 and 22.1: the amount of the allowance, the effect on the pensioner's
-- supplement, and the additional amounts. Piece oa2.
--
-- The amounts are formulas in the Act's own letters (A, B, C, D, E). Incomes are NUMBERS for the base calendar year
-- (the keel's `the income of a person for a calendar year`, or section 13 for a month before July 1, 1999); the
-- pension equivalent is an input from section 7 (piece oa1) and the Consumer Price Index figures are inputs, as in
-- section 12. A formula that comes out below nothing is floored in a wrapper rule, the raw formula being kept
-- (fork F-12-2); a bracket that the text leaves open at zero is closed at zero and tested (finding in NOTES.md).
-- Rounding to the cent and of the CPI ratio is Regulations s 8 (piece oa3) and is not applied.

§ `Part III -- Monthly Allowances`

§§ `Definitions, section 22(1)`

-- "base calendar year has the same meaning as in section 10"
-- src:644 | base calendar year has the same meaning as in section 10; (année de référence)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "base calendar year" (src:644)
GIVEN `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`s 22(1): the base calendar year` `the current payment period` MEANS
    `s 10: the base calendar year` `the current payment period`

-- "current payment period means the payment period in respect of which an application for an allowance is made under
-- this Part"
-- src:646 | current payment period means the payment period in respect of which an application for an allowance is made under this Part; (période de paiement en cours)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "current payment period" (src:646)
GIVEN `a month in the payment period in respect of which the application for an allowance is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`s 22(1): the current payment period` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the application for an allowance is made` MEANS
    `the payment period in relation to the month containing` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the application for an allowance is made`

-- "income, for the purposes of determining the amount of benefits under this Part that may be paid for a month before
-- July 1, 1999, means the income calculated as prescribed by section 13"
-- src:647 | income, for the purposes of determining the amount of benefits under this Part that may be paid for a month before July 1, 1999, means the income calculated as prescribed by section 13; (revenu de l’année civile)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "income" (src:647)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 22(1): the income for a month before July 1, 1999` month facts MEANS
    `s 13: the income of a person for a calendar year, for a month before July 1, 1999` month facts

-- "monthly income of a survivor in a current payment period is the amount that equals one-twelfth of their income for
-- the base calendar year"
-- src:648 | monthly income of a survivor in a current payment period is the amount that equals one-twelfth of their income for the base calendar year; (revenu mensuel du survivant)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "monthly income of a survivor" (src:648)
GIVEN `the survivor's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the monthly income of a survivor` `the survivor's income for the base calendar year` MEANS
    `the survivor's income for the base calendar year` DIVIDED BY 12

-- "monthly joint income of a pensioner and their spouse or common-law partner in a current payment period is the
-- amount that equals 1/12 of the total of both of their incomes for the base calendar year; however, for the purpose
-- of calculating the allowance that may be paid to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner under subsection (3)
-- for either of the following periods, it is the amount that equals 1/12 of the income of the spouse or common-law
-- partner for the base calendar year: (a) the months during which the pensioner is an incarcerated person described
-- in subsection 5(3), exclusive of the first month of incarceration and the month of release; or (b) if a direction
-- made under subsection 19(8) in respect of the spouse or common-law partner has not been cancelled under subsection
-- 19(9), the months, exclusive of the first month, during which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with
-- the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them"
-- (a): the month is after the first month of incarceration and before the month of release.
-- src:650 | (a) the months during which the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3), exclusive of the first month of incarceration and the month of release; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a) (src:650)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
      `the first month of incarceration` IS A DATE
      `the month of release` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` month `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `the first month of incarceration` `the month of release` MEANS
        `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the first month of incarceration`
    AND CONSIDER `the month of release`
        WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` released
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- (b): the direction under 19(8) has not been cancelled under 19(9); the months after the first month in which the
-- spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one of them.
-- src:651 | (b) if a direction made under subsection 19(8) in respect of the spouse or common-law partner has not been cancelled under subsection 19(9), the months, exclusive of the first month, during which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them; (revenu conjoint mensuel)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b) (src:651)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `a direction made under subsection 19(8) in respect of the spouse or common-law partner has not been cancelled under subsection 19(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first month in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` month `a direction made under subsection 19(8) in respect of the spouse or common-law partner has not been cancelled under subsection 19(9)` `the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them` `the first month in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner` MEANS
        `a direction made under subsection 19(8) in respect of the spouse or common-law partner has not been cancelled under subsection 19(9)`
    AND `the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the first month in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner`

-- src:649 | monthly joint income of a pensioner and their spouse or common-law partner in a current payment period is the amount that equals 1/12 of the total of both of their incomes for the base calendar year; however, for the purpose of calculating the allowance that may be paid to the pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner under subsection (3) for either of the following periods, it is the amount that equals 1/12 of the income of the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year:
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (src:649)
GIVEN `the pensioner's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the month is one of the months in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the monthly joint income` `the pensioner's income for the base calendar year` `the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` `the month is one of the months in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition` MEANS
    IF `the month is one of the months in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition`
    THEN `the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` DIVIDED BY 12
    ELSE (`the pensioner's income for the base calendar year` PLUS `the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- "pension equivalent means, in respect of any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the full monthly pension
-- payable for that month under section 7 that has not been increased under subsection 7(5)"
-- src:652 | pension equivalent means, in respect of any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the full monthly pension payable for that month under section 7 that has not been increased under subsection 7(5); (valeur de la pension)
