`s 22(1): the rounded pension equivalent` `the pension equivalent` MEANS
    `the pension equivalent` `rounded to the next higher multiple of` 3

-- "rounded supplement equivalent means the supplement equivalent rounded to the next higher multiple of one dollar
-- when the supplement equivalent is not a multiple of one dollar"
-- src:668 | rounded supplement equivalent means the supplement equivalent rounded to the next higher multiple of one dollar when the supplement equivalent is not a multiple of one dollar; (valeur arrondie du supplément)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "rounded supplement equivalent" (src:668)
GIVEN `the supplement equivalent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the rounded supplement equivalent` `the supplement equivalent` MEANS
    `the supplement equivalent` `rounded to the next higher multiple of` 1

-- "supplement equivalent means, in respect of any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the supplement that would
-- be payable for that month under subsection 12(1), (1.1), (1.2), (2), (3) or (4), as the case may be, to a
-- pensioner whose spouse or common-law partner is also a pensioner when both the pensioner and the spouse or
-- common-law partner have no income in the base calendar year and both are in receipt of a full pension"
-- That pensioner is in paragraph 12(1)(b)(ii), with no income to reduce the maximum: the supplement equivalent is the
-- maximum for that paragraph. For the quarter commencing on April 1, 2005 it is 366.67; later quarters are worked out
-- by the rules of section 12 for the situation of 12(1)(b)(ii).
-- src:669 | supplement equivalent means, in respect of any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the supplement that would be payable for that month under subsection 12(1), (1.1), (1.2), (2), (3) or (4), as the case may be, to a pensioner whose spouse or common-law partner is also a pensioner when both the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner have no income in the base calendar year and both are in receipt of a full pension; (valeur du supplément)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "supplement equivalent" (April 1, 2005) (src:669)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for the payment quarter commencing on April 1, 2005` MEANS
    `s 12(1): the maximum supplement for the payment quarter commencing on April 1, 2005` `s 12(1)(b)(ii): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has a pension payable from this month`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "supplement equivalent" (src:669)
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE
      `the supplement equivalent for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter`
`s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` `the first day of the payment quarter` `the supplement equivalent for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` MEANS
    `s 12(2): the maximum supplement for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005`
        `the first day of the payment quarter`
        `s 12(1)(b)(ii): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has a pension payable from this month`
        `the supplement equivalent for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter`
        `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
        `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
        `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`

-- "supplement equivalent for the survivor means, in respect of any month in a payment quarter, the amount
-- determined under subsection (4.1), (4.2), (4.3) or (4.4), as the case may be": see subsections (4.1) to (4.4) below.

-- "residual income of the survivor for a month in a current payment period means the amount determined by the formula
-- A - B where A is the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period, and B is the product (a)
-- obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent by the survivor's special qualifying factor
-- for the month, and (b) rounded, where that product is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple
-- of four dollars"
-- src:653 | residual income of the survivor for a month in a current payment period means the amount determined by the formula
-- src:654 | A - B
-- src:655 | where
-- src:656 | A is the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period, and
-- src:657 | B is the product
-- src:658 | (a) obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent by the survivor’s special qualifying factor for the month, and
-- src:659 | (b) rounded, where that product is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple of four dollars; (revenu résiduel du survivant)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "residual income of the survivor" (src:653-659)
GIVEN `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period` IS A NUMBER
      `the rounded pension equivalent` IS A NUMBER
      `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the residual income of the survivor` `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period` `the rounded pension equivalent` `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month` MEANS
    `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period` MINUS ((((4 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES `the rounded pension equivalent`) TIMES `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month`) `rounded to the next higher multiple of` 4)

-- "residual joint income of a pensioner and the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for a month in a current
-- payment period means the amount determined by the formula A - B where A is the monthly joint income [...] and B is
-- the product (a) obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent by the spouse's or
-- common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month, and (b) rounded, where that product is not a
-- multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple of four dollars"
-- src:660 | residual joint income of a pensioner and the pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner for a month in a current payment period means the amount determined by the formula
-- src:661 | A - B
-- src:662 | where
-- src:663 | A is the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period, and
-- src:664 | B is the product
-- src:665 | (a) obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent by the spouse’s or common-law partner’s special qualifying factor for the month, and
-- src:666 | (b) rounded, where that product is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple of four dollars; (revenu conjoint résiduel)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(1) "residual joint income" (src:660-666)
GIVEN `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period` IS A NUMBER
      `the rounded pension equivalent` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(1): the residual joint income` `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period` `the rounded pension equivalent` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` MEANS
    `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period` MINUS ((((4 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES `the rounded pension equivalent`) TIMES `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month`) `rounded to the next higher multiple of` 4)

§§ `Effect on the supplement of the pensioner, subsection 22(2)`

-- (2) "Where, under this Part, an application has been made and approved or the requirement for an application has
-- been waived in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner for any month in a payment quarter, the
-- amount of the supplement that may be paid for that month to the pensioner, in lieu of the amount of the supplement
-- provided under Part II for that month, is the amount determined by the formula [(A - B) x C] - D/4 where A is the
-- total of the supplement equivalent in respect of that month and the amount of the full monthly pension for that
-- month; B is the pensioner's monthly pension for that month; C is the pensioner's special qualifying factor for that
-- month; and D is the residual joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for that month
-- rounded, where that income is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars."
-- src:672 | (2) Where, under this Part, an application has been made and approved or the requirement for an application has been waived in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner for any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the supplement that may be paid for that month to the pensioner, in lieu of the amount of the supplement provided under Part II for that month, is the amount determined by the formula
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(2) condition (src:672)
GIVEN `an application has been made and approved under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement for an application has been waived under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2): the supplement under this subsection is payable in lieu of the supplement under Part II` `an application has been made and approved under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month` `the requirement for an application has been waived under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month` MEANS
    `an application has been made and approved under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month` OR `the requirement for an application has been waived under this Part in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner for the month`

-- src:672 | (2) Where, under this Part, an application has been made and approved or the requirement for an application has been waived in respect of the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner for any month in a payment quarter, the amount of the supplement that may be paid for that month to the pensioner, in lieu of the amount of the supplement provided under Part II for that month, is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:673 | [(A - B) × C] - D/4
-- src:674 | where
-- src:675 | A is the total of the supplement equivalent in respect of that month and the amount of the full monthly pension for that month;
-- src:676 | B is the pensioner’s monthly pension for that month;
-- src:677 | C is the pensioner’s special qualifying factor for that month; and
-- src:678 | D is the residual joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for that month rounded, where that income is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(2) formula (src:672-678)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: sections 7 and 7.1 (piece oa1)
      `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: sections 7 and 7.1 (piece oa1)
      `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: sections 7 and 7.1 (piece oa1)
      `the pensioner's monthly pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: sections 7 and 7.1 (piece oa1)
      `the pensioner's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the residual joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` month `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pensioner's special qualification facts` `the residual joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the month` MEANS
    ((partA MINUS partB) TIMES partC) MINUS (partD DIVIDED BY 4)
    WHERE
        partA MEANS `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` PLUS `the amount of a full monthly pension` `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`
        partB MEANS `the pensioner's monthly pension in subsections 12(5) and 22(2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`
        partC MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the pensioner's special qualification facts`
        partD MEANS `the residual joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the month` `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- The supplement that "may be paid" is not a negative sum: where the formula comes out below nothing, nothing may be
-- paid (fork F-12-2, as for section 12(5)).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(2) (src:672-678)
GIVEN formula IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(2): the amount of the supplement that may be paid, given the formula` formula MEANS
    max 0 formula

-- (2.1) "No supplement under subsection (2) may be paid to an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) for any
-- month for which no pension may be paid."
-- src:680 | (2.1) No supplement under subsection (2) may be paid to an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) for any month for which no pension may be paid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(2.1) (src:680)
GIVEN `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
      `no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2.1): a supplement under subsection 22(2) may not be paid` `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` MEANS
    `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` AND `no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month`

§§ `Allowance to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner, subsection 22(3)`

-- The product used by the branches: "(i) obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent in
-- respect of the month by the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month, and (ii)
-- rounded, where that product is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple of four dollars".
-- src:686 | (b) where the monthly joint income of the pensioner and spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period is equal to or less than the product
-- src:687 | (i) obtained by multiplying four-thirds of the rounded pension equivalent in respect of the month by the spouse’s or common-law partner’s special qualifying factor for the month, and
-- src:688 | (ii) rounded, where that product is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next higher multiple of four dollars,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(3)(b)(i), (ii) (src:686-688)
GIVEN `the rounded pension equivalent` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(3)(b): the product against which the monthly joint income is measured` `the rounded pension equivalent` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` MEANS
    (((4 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES `the rounded pension equivalent`) TIMES `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month`) `rounded to the next higher multiple of` 4

-- (a) "where there is no monthly joint income of the pensioner and spouse or common-law partner in the current
-- payment period, the total of (i) the product obtained by multiplying the pension equivalent in respect of the month
-- by the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month, and (ii) the product obtained by
-- multiplying the supplement equivalent in respect of the month by the spouse's or common-law partner's special
-- qualifying factor for the month"
-- src:683 | (a) where there is no monthly joint income of the pensioner and spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period, the total of
-- src:684 | (i) the product obtained by multiplying the pension equivalent in respect of the month by the spouse’s or common-law partner’s special qualifying factor for the month, and
-- src:685 | (ii) the product obtained by multiplying the supplement equivalent in respect of the month by the spouse’s or common-law partner’s special qualifying factor for the month;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(3)(a) (src:683-685)
GIVEN `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(3)(a): the amount of the allowance` `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` MEANS
        `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` TIMES `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month`
    PLUS `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` TIMES `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month`

-- (b) "where the monthly joint income [...] is equal to or less than the product [...] the amount determined by the
-- formula (A x B) + C where A is the supplement equivalent in respect of the month, B is the spouse's or common-law
-- partner's special qualifying factor for the month, and C is the greater of zero and the amount determined by the
-- formula (D x B) - 3/4 E where B is [the same factor], D is the pension equivalent in respect of the month, and E is
