    ELSE 0

-- (4.2), (4.3), (4.4) "for any month in a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005 [...] the amount obtained by
-- multiplying (a) the amount of the supplement equivalent for the survivor for any month in the three-month period
-- immediately before that payment quarter by (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment
-- quarter [...] bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter"; not less than the amount for the
-- previous quarter; no adjustment after a fall until the index recovers, the earlier second index then being deemed
-- the second index. The fixed increases of (4.1)(b) and (c) are added for those two quarters.
-- src:743 | (4.2) Subject to paragraphs (4.1)(b) and (c), the amount of the supplement equivalent for the survivor for any month in a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005 is the amount obtained by multiplying
-- src:744 | (a) the amount of the supplement equivalent for the survivor for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter
-- src:745 | by
-- src:746 | (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter.
-- src:747 | No decrease
-- src:748 | (4.3) Despite subsection (4.2), the amount of the supplement equivalent for the survivor for any month in a payment quarter may not be less than the amount of the supplement equivalent for the survivor for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter.
-- src:749 | Reduction in Consumer Price Index
-- src:750 | (4.4) If, in relation to any payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter is lower than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter,
-- src:751 | (a) no adjustment of the supplement equivalent for the survivor is to be made under subsection (4.2) in respect of that payment quarter; and
-- src:752 | (b) no adjustment of the supplement equivalent for the survivor is to be made under that subsection in respect of any subsequent payment quarter until, in relation to a subsequent payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter is higher than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in paragraph (a), in which case the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in that paragraph is deemed to be the second adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(4.2), s 22(4.3), s 22(4.4) (src:743-752)
