§§ `Reinstatement of the supplement, subsections 22(5) to 22(7)`

-- (5) "Where the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner under this Part is suspended or
-- terminated for any month, the pensioner may, notwithstanding subsection (2), be paid, for that month, the amount of
-- supplement provided under Part II."
-- src:754 | (5) Where the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner under this Part is suspended or terminated for any month, the pensioner may, notwithstanding subsection (2), be paid, for that month, the amount of supplement provided under Part II.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(5) (src:754)
GIVEN `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is suspended for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is terminated for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(5): the pensioner may be paid the amount of supplement provided under Part II for the month` `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is suspended for the month` `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is terminated for the month` MEANS
    `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is suspended for the month` OR `the allowance payable to the spouse or common-law partner of the pensioner under this Part is terminated for the month`

-- (6) "Where, by reason of the amount of the monthly joint income, the aggregate of the amount of allowance payable to
-- a pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for a month and the amount of supplement payable to the pensioner for
-- that month under this Part is less than the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part
-- II, the pensioner may, notwithstanding subsection (2), be paid, for that month, the amount of supplement provided
-- under Part II minus the amount, if any, of allowance payable to that pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for
-- that month."
-- src:756 | (6) Where, by reason of the amount of the monthly joint income, the aggregate of the amount of allowance payable to a pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner for a month and the amount of supplement payable to the pensioner for that month under this Part is less than the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part II, the pensioner may, notwithstanding subsection (2), be paid, for that month, the amount of supplement provided under Part II minus the amount, if any, of allowance payable to that pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner for that month.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(6) (src:756)
GIVEN `the amount of allowance payable to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of supplement payable to the pensioner for the month under this Part` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part II for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 22(6): the amount of supplement the pensioner may be paid for the month` `the amount of allowance payable to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for the month` `the amount of supplement payable to the pensioner for the month under this Part` `the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part II for the month` MEANS
    IF `the amount of allowance payable to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for the month` PLUS `the amount of supplement payable to the pensioner for the month under this Part` LESS THAN `the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part II for the month`
    THEN JUST (`the amount of supplement that would be payable to the pensioner under Part II for the month` MINUS `the amount of allowance payable to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner for the month`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7) "For the purposes of subsections (5) and (6), an application made and approved under this Part shall be deemed
-- to have been made and approved under Part II."
-- src:758 | (7) For the purposes of subsections (5) and (6), an application made and approved under this Part shall be deemed to have been made and approved under Part II.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22(7) (src:758)
GIVEN `an application has been made and approved under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(7): the application is deemed to have been made and approved under Part II` `an application has been made and approved under this Part` MEANS
    `an application has been made and approved under this Part`

§§ `Additional amounts, section 22.1`

-- The quarterly chain of A in subsections 22.1(1) to (3): "A is $35" (subsections (1) and (2)), "A is $50"
-- (subsection (3)) for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011; then, "for any month in a payment quarter
-- beginning after September 30, 2011", the amount for the quarter before multiplied by the ratio of the Consumer Price
-- Index for the first adjustment quarter to that for the second (4), never less than the amount for the quarter
-- before (5), with no adjustment after a fall in the index until it recovers, the earlier second index then deemed the
-- second index (6); and for the quarter beginning on July 1, 2016 the amount determined for A in subsection (3) is
-- that amount plus $78.92 (3.1).
-- One rule does all three; the three subsections each wrap it with their own amount of A. The quarter beginning on
-- July 1, 2011 (the first "beginning after June 30, 2011") has the opening amount; a quarter that begins on or before
-- June 30, 2011 is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:783 | (4) Subject to subsection (3.1), for the purpose of calculating the amount payable under any of subsections (1) to (3) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after September 30, 2011, the amount to be determined for A in that subsection is the amount obtained by multiplying
-- src:784 | (a) the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter
-- src:785 | by
-- src:786 | (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter.
-- src:787 | No decrease
-- src:788 | (5) Despite subsection (4), the amount determined for A for any month in a payment quarter shall not be less than the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter.
-- src:789 | Effect of reduction in Consumer Price Index
-- src:790 | (6) If, in relation to any payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter is lower than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter,
-- src:791 | (a) no adjustment to the amount determined for A shall be made under subsection (4) in respect of that payment quarter; and
-- src:792 | (b) no adjustment to the amount determined for A shall be made under subsection (4) in respect of any subsequent payment quarter until, in relation to a subsequent payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter is higher than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in paragraph (a), in which case the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in that paragraph is deemed to be the second adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(4), s 22.1(5), s 22.1(6) (src:783-792)
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE
      `the opening amount of A` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase on July 1, 2016` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter`
`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` `the first day of the payment quarter` `the opening amount of A` `the increase on July 1, 2016` `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first day of the payment quarter` AT MOST (YMD 2011 6 30)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the first day of the payment quarter` AT MOST (YMD 2011 9 30)
        THEN JUST (`oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter` WITH
                       `the amount for the payment quarter` IS `the opening amount of A`
                       `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS NOTHING)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter` WITH
                       `the amount for the payment quarter` IS indexed's `the amount for the payment quarter` PLUS fixedIncrease
                       `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS indexed's `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`)
    WHERE
        indexed MEANS
            `oa2 indexation: the outcome for a payment quarter`
                `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`
        fixedIncrease MEANS
            IF `the first day of the payment quarter` EQUALS (YMD 2016 7 1)
            THEN `the increase on July 1, 2016`
            ELSE 0

-- (3.1) "The amount determined for A in subsection (3) for any month in the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016
-- is the amount that would otherwise have been determined for A in that subsection for any month in that payment
-- quarter plus $78.92." Only subsection (3)'s A (the survivor's) is increased.
-- src:781 | (3.1) The amount determined for A in subsection (3) for any month in the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016 is the amount that would otherwise have been determined for A in that subsection for any month in that payment quarter plus $78.92.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(3.1) (src:781)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22.1(3.1): the increase on July 1, 2016 for A in subsection 22.1(3)` MEANS 78.92

-- (3) The survivor's A: $50 for the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2011, then as above with the increase of
-- (3.1) in the quarter beginning on July 1, 2016.
