-- (1) "The amount that may be added to the amount of the supplement that may be paid to a pensioner referred to in
-- subsection 22(2) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the
-- formula A x B - C/4 where A is $35; B is the pensioner's special qualifying factor for the month; and C is 1/24 of
-- the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year
-- in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars."
-- The rounding is read as applying to the monthly figure that results (fork F-12.1-1, as for section 12.1).
-- src:760 | 22.1 (1) The amount that may be added to the amount of the supplement that may be paid to a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:761 | A × B – C/4
-- src:762 | where
-- src:763 | A is $35;
-- src:764 | B is the pensioner’s special qualifying factor for the month; and
-- src:765 | C is 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(1) (src:760-765)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER
      `the pensioner's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2)` month `the amount determined for A` `the pensioner's special qualification facts` `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MEANS
    (`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (reductionC DIVIDED BY 4)
    WHERE
        factorB MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the pensioner's special qualification facts`
        reductionC MEANS ((max 0 (`the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MINUS 4000)) DIVIDED BY 24) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- (2) "The amount that may be added to the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a spouse or common-law partner
-- referred to in subsection 22(3) [...] A x B - C/4 where A is $35; B is the special qualifying factor for the spouse
-- or common-law partner for the month; and C is 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her
-- spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded [...] to the next lower
-- multiple of four dollars."
-- src:767 | (2) The amount that may be added to the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:768 | A × B – C/4
-- src:769 | where
-- src:770 | A is $35;
-- src:771 | B is the special qualifying factor for the spouse or common-law partner for the month; and
-- src:772 | C is 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(2) (src:767-772)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3)` month `the amount determined for A` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualification facts` `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MEANS
    (`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (reductionC DIVIDED BY 4)
    WHERE
        factorB MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualification facts`
        reductionC MEANS ((max 0 (`the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MINUS 4000)) DIVIDED BY 24) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- (3) "The amount that may be added to the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor referred to in
-- subsection 22(4) [...] A x B - C/4 where A is $50; B is the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month; and
-- C is 1/12 of the survivor's income for the base calendar year in excess of $2,000 rounded [...] to the next lower
-- multiple of four dollars."
-- src:774 | (3) The amount that may be added to the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:775 | A × B – C/4
-- src:776 | where
-- src:777 | A is $50;
-- src:778 | B is the survivor’s special qualifying factor for the month; and
-- src:779 | C is 1/12 of the survivor’s income for the base calendar year in excess of $2,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(3) (src:774-779)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER
      `the survivor's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the survivor's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` month `the amount determined for A` `the survivor's special qualification facts` `the survivor's income for the base calendar year` MEANS
    (`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (reductionC DIVIDED BY 4)
    WHERE
        factorB MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the survivor's special qualification facts`
        reductionC MEANS ((max 0 (`the survivor's income for the base calendar year` MINUS 2000)) DIVIDED BY 12) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- The amount "that may be added" is not a negative sum: where the formula comes out below nothing, nothing is added
-- (fork F-12-2, as for sections 12(5) and 12.1).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 22.1(1), s 22.1(2), s 22.1(3) (src:760-779)
GIVEN formula IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` formula MEANS
    max 0 formula
